content.text:
`fetchMock` no longer exists in current versions. The Vitest 3 → 4 migration guide says: *"The `import { fetchMock } from "cloudflare:test"` import has been removed."* Cloudflare now recommends MSW through `@msw/cloudflare`. The package has also been renamed from `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` to `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`, version 1, as of 2026-08-19. There's a codemod for the rename: `npx @cloudflare/codemods vitest:pool-workers-to-vitest-plugin`.

## Current approach (Vitest 4 / `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`)

```sh
npm i -D msw@^2.14.0 @msw/cloudflare
```

**`test/network.ts`**, a shared network mock:
```ts
import { setupNetwork } from "@msw/cloudflare";

export const network = setupNetwork();
```

**`test/setup.ts`**. Add this file to `setupFiles` in your Vitest config:
```ts
import { afterAll, afterEach, beforeAll } from "vitest";
import { network } from "./network";

beforeAll(() => network.enable());
afterEach(() => network.resetHandlers());
afterAll(() => network.disable());
```

**`test/worker.test.ts`**:
```ts
import { createExecutionContext, waitOnExecutionContext } from "cloudflare:test";
import { env } from "cloudflare:workers";
import { http, HttpResponse } from "msw";
import { expect, it } from "vitest";
import worker from "../src";
import { network } from "./network";

it("mocks an outbound request", async () => {
  network.use(
    http.get("https://api.example.com/greeting", () =>
      HttpResponse.json({ message: "Hello" }),
    ),
  );

  const ctx = createExecutionContext();
  const response = await worker.fetch(new Request("https://example.com"), env, ctx);
  await waitOnExecutionContext(ctx);
  expect(await response.json()).toEqual({ message: "Hello" });
});
```

To mock outbound WebSockets, use MSW's `ws.link()`. If you don't want MSW at all, the migration guide also says you can mock `globalThis.fetch` directly, for example with `vi.spyOn(globalThis, "fetch")`.

**Caveats:**
- `@msw/cloudflare` is a very new package. One third-party write-up says it's at version 0.0.1, has no license file, and has a peer-range conflict with `msw@^2.14.0`. I couldn't confirm that, so check it if npm complains when you install.
- Some tutorials, such as Mintlify-hosted docs, still show `fetchMock`. Those examples are outdated.

## Legacy approach (older `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` on Vitest 3)

If you're still on the old package, `fetchMock` is an undici `MockAgent`. This snippet comes from the API I remember, not from the pages I checked this time:

```ts
import { fetchMock } from "cloudflare:test";
import { beforeAll, afterEach } from "vitest";

beforeAll(() => {
  fetchMock.activate();
  fetchMock.disableNetConnect(); // fail on any unmocked request
});
afterEach(() => fetchMock.assertNoPendingInterceptors());

it("mocks", async () => {
  fetchMock
    .get("https://api.example.com")
    .intercept({ path: "/greeting" })
    .reply(200, { message: "Hello" });
  // ...call your worker
});
```

Once you upgrade, plan to move to MSW. Separately, `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` 0.20.0 also removed a `fetchMock` option from the `miniflare` pool options and replaced it with `outboundService`.

Sources:
- [Mock outbound requests – Cloudflare docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/mock-outbound-requests/)
- [Migrate from Vitest 3 to Vitest 4 – Cloudflare docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/migration-guides/migrate-from-vitest-3-to-vitest-4/)
- [@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers is now @cloudflare/vitest-plugin – changelog](https://docs-durable-objects-instance-replaced-errors.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-08-19-vitest-plugin/)
- [vitest-pool-workers 0.20.0 release notes](https://newreleases.io/project/github/cloudflare/workers-sdk/release/@cloudflare%2Fvitest-pool-workers@0.20.0)
- [Third-party analysis of the vitest-plugin 1.0 / MSW peer conflict](https://ecorpit.com/cloudflare-vitest-plugin-1-0-msw-peer-dependency-conflict-2026/)

